VeridianOS: mark Manager::serviceOwnerChanged()'s unused newOwner parameter

GCC reported -Wunused-parameter for 'newOwner' in src/lib/manager_p.cpp. The
slot re-queries the bus for the service state instead of using the owner
arguments; it already marks oldOwner with Q_UNUSED, and now marks newOwner
the same way. Behaviour is unchanged.

diff -ru a/src/lib/manager_p.cpp b/src/lib/manager_p.cpp
--- a/src/lib/manager_p.cpp	2026-10-08 17:00:33.244735099 -0400
+++ b/src/lib/manager_p.cpp	2026-10-08 17:00:42.336048667 -0400
@@ -92,6 +92,7 @@
 void Manager::serviceOwnerChanged(const QString &serviceName, const QString &oldOwner, const QString &newOwner)
 {
     Q_UNUSED(oldOwner);
+    Q_UNUSED(newOwner);
 
     if (serviceName == KAMD_DBUS_SERVICE) {
         const bool isRunning = QDBusConnection::sessionBus().interface()->isServiceRegistered(KAMD_DBUS_SERVICE);
